        <section class="settings-card wide"><h2>Console games & emulation</h2><div class="settings-row"><div><div class="settings-label">Console Games service</div><div class="settings-help">RomM + bundled EmulatorJS, managed by PCGA.</div></div><div class="settings-control"><input id="cc-romm-enabled" type="checkbox"></div></div><div class="settings-row"><div><div class="settings-label">Automatic ROM discovery</div><div class="settings-help">Watch the canonical ROM library and scan after copies settle.</div></div><div class="settings-control"><input id="cc-romm-watch" type="checkbox"></div></div><div class="settings-row"><div><div class="settings-label">Discovery settle delay</div></div><div class="settings-control"><select id="cc-romm-debounce"><option value="60">1 minute</option><option value="180">3 minutes</option><option value="300">5 minutes</option><option value="600">10 minutes</option><option value="900">15 minutes</option></select></div></div><div class="settings-row"><div><div class="settings-label">Hasheous metadata</div></div><div class="settings-control"><input id="cc-hasheous" type="checkbox"></div></div><div class="settings-row"><div><div class="settings-label">PlayMatch metadata</div></div><div class="settings-control"><input id="cc-playmatch" type="checkbox"></div></div><div class="control-actions"><button class="control-button" data-control-action="restart:romm" type="button">Restart Console Games</button></div><div class="settings-note">PCGA creates the ROM/BIOS/database/resource structure automatically. Native RomM setup is treated as an advanced escape hatch, not a required appliance step.</div></section>
        <section class="settings-card wide"><h2>PC games & LAN sessions</h2><div class="settings-row"><div><div class="settings-label">LANCommander appliance service</div><div class="settings-help">Pinned and initialized by PCGA; its native administration UI is available under Advanced.</div></div><div class="settings-control"><span class="badge">Managed</span></div></div><div class="settings-row"><div><div class="settings-label">Browser stream transport</div><div class="settings-help">Automatic preflights H.264 WebCodecs support and prefers WebSocket + WebCodecs; WebRTC remains the fallback and an optional low-latency path.</div></div><div class="settings-control"><select id="setting-pc-game-transport"><option value="auto">Automatic (recommended)</option><option value="websocket">WebSocket + WebCodecs</option><option value="webrtc">WebRTC (low latency)</option></select></div></div><div class="control-actions"><button class="control-button" data-control-action="restart:lancommander" type="button">Restart PC Games</button></div><div class="settings-note">PCGA owns first-run initialization and keeps LANCommander on a tested version so upgrades cannot unexpectedly reintroduce onboarding.</div></section>
